{"claim":"MEMO","check":"B","status":"misstate","reason":"The memo's Why this is safe says the whole lane is self-contained because its dependencies are internal and quotes \"no non-KCPT document is a load-bearing dependency\". The primary KCPT_CORNER_CARRIER_TWO_PRESENTATION_SWAP_PROPER_ROTATION_CONJUGACY note instead explicitly consumes two non-KCPT dependencies: MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md supplies the proper cubic rotation group and admissibility covariance, and STAGGERED_DIRAC_REALIZATION_GATE_NOTE_2026-05-03.md names the operator surface; both appear in its Dependencies list. The self-containment rationale is therefore false as written, independently of whether those external dependencies are retained or open."}
{"claim":"MEMO","check":"C","status":"contested","reason":"The memo's \"Deltas this memo carries\" omits the load-bearing Berezin-probe theorem of KCPT_COUPLING_TRIPLE_BEREZIN_COUNT_BINARY_MEASURE_COLLAPSE: under the pinned measure the quadratic integral is exactly det M (with reversed ordering giving (-1)^n det M); horn m uses 6m generators; every active constant homogeneous odd-linear substitution at fixed count/held measure multiplies the zero-source output by det S, while the explicitly computed coupling-dependent substitution A(W)=W converts det3 to det3^2. The Arc merely labels this \"Berezin count-binary measure collapse\" and neither states these results nor points to the primary. LIVE_SURFACES names the AC occupancy obligation but carries none of these exact finite-surface results."}
{"claim":"MEMO","check":"B","status":"misstate","reason":"The D2-commutant delta states the exact object \"|Comm| = 96N\" without a size qualifier. The primary KCPT_D2_COMMUTANT_CLOSED_FORM_LIFTS_AND_LATTICE_SIZE_INDEPENDENCE note explicitly limits equality to exhaustive L in {4,6,8,10}; at L=12 it proves only \"|Comm(D2)| >= 96N = 165888\" and says equality is NOT established, while its general even-L result covers only the translation lifts/commutator/q formulas. The memo thus drops a load-bearing scope boundary and overstates the equality."}
